=== layout: two-panels
@replaceme

# *Summary of Sex Determination in Fruit Flies*

@left

![Slide image 21](assets/lect11c-sex_dosage/image_021.png)

@right

- [metafemale]{color=red} (or superfemale) is a low viability Drosophila with a female phenotype [(X\:A ratio > 1)]{color=red}
- [metamale]{color=blue} (or supermale) is a low viability Drosophila with a male phenotype [(X\:A ratio < &#189;)]{color=blue}
- [intersex]{color=#800080} are are individuals born that do not fit the typical definitions for male or female bodies [(&#189; < X\:A ratio < 1)]{color=#800080}

=== layout: two-panels
@replaceme

# *Sex determination*

@left

- Nomenclature\:
  - X = female sex chromosome
  - A = autosomes
- Hypothesis\:
  - ratio of 1 is female
  - ratio of &#189; is male
  - ratio in between is intersex

@right

- X\:AA ratio of 0.5
  - Diploid with 1 X
  - [normal male]{color=blue}
- XX\:AAA ratio of 0.67
  - Triploid with 2 X
  - [intersex]{color=#800080}
- XX\:AA ratio of 1.0
  - Diploid with 2 X
  - [normal female]{color=red}
- X\:A ratio of 1
  - Haploid with 1 X
  - [initially female then dies]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Sex determination*

@body

- Nomenclature\:
  - X = female sex chromosome
  - A = autosomes
- Hypothesis\:
  - ratio of 1 is female
  - ratio of &#189; is male
  - ratio in between is intersex
  - ratio > 1 is [metafemale]{color=orange} or super female
  - ratio < 0.5 is [metamale]{color=green} or super male

- X\:AAA, ratio of 0.33
  - Triploid with 1 X
  - [metamale]{color=green}, low viability
- X\:AA, ratio of 0.5
  - Diploid with 1 X
  - [normal male]{color=blue}
- XX\:AAA, ratio of 0.67
  - Triploid with 2 X
  - [intersex]{color=#800080}
- X\:A, ratio of 1.0
  - Haploid with 1 X
  - [initially female then dies]{color=red}
- XX\:AA, ratio of 1.0
  - Diploid with 2 X
  - [normal female]{color=red}
- XXX\:AA, ratio of 1.5
  - Diploid with 3 X
  - [metafemale]{color=orange}, low viability

- [*more female*]{color=red}
- [*higher X/A ratio*]{color=red}

=== layout: two-panels
@replaceme

# *Note on Nomenclature*

@left

- normal drosophila females are 8,XX
  - 8 chromosomes total and 2 X chromosomes
    - 2,2,3,3,4,4,X,X
- XX\:AAA
  - this drosophila would be 11,XX
    - 11 chromosomes total and 2 X chromosomes
      - 2,2,2,3,3,3,4,4,4,X,X
  - AAA means that the organism is triploid, 3n, three copies of every chromosome
    - so in drosophila\:
      - 3 copies of chromosome 2
      - 3 copies of chromosome 3
      - 3 copies of chromosome 4
  - but they would only have two X chromosomes

@right

![Slide image 22](assets/visual_renewal/ploidy_sets.drawn.svg)

- A

- AA

- AAA

- `AAAA`

